WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:06.720
three common openings for white you should know a&nbsp;
common way a game begins is with the solid move e4&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:14.080
controlling the center black typically responds e5&nbsp;
the game frequently continues with knight f3 and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:21.120
knight c6 then usually one of three popular&nbsp;
moves bishop c4 known as the italian game&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:28.640
black often responds bishop c5 you could also play&nbsp;
bishop b5 which is known as the roy lopez opening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:36.400
a popular response for black is a6 white typically&nbsp;
retreats the bishop to a4 and if attacked again&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:40.640
moves the bishop to b3 which&nbsp;
attacks the weak f7 pawn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:45.920
instead of bringing out the bishop white can&nbsp;
also play d4 putting pressure on the e pawn and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:50.800
opening lines for the queen and dark squared&nbsp;
bishop this is known as the scotch opening

